    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2622" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănĭmātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>he
				that quickens</i> or <i>animates</i> (post-class., oftenest in the Church fathers): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 48</span></i>
			; so Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10,
				788.—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marmoris signifex animator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Capitol. 1, p. 13</span></i>
			.</div>
